    <!-- Key Takeaways -->
    <section class="section" id="takeaways">
      <span class="section-label">Summary</span>
      <h2>Key Takeaways</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Accuracy is dangerous on imbalanced data</strong> — always use class-aware metrics like precision, recall, and F1</li>
        <li><strong>Precision vs Recall is a fundamental tradeoff</strong> — choose based on which error is more costly in your domain</li>
        <li><strong>ROC-AUC for ranking ability</strong> — use to evaluate how well your model separates positive and negative cases</li>
        <li><strong>Context matters</strong> — the "best" metric depends entirely on your business requirements and the cost of different errors</li>
        <li><strong>Always use confusion matrix visualization</strong> — it provides immediate intuition about your model's performance</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

